okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Codex launches with no reasoning effort get medium: (1) a launch-time -c default for native Codex, (2) the launch config.toml gets a top-level default before Codex starts (TUI, app-server, remote TUI, desktop app)."
reported: "User, 2026-10-08: '코덱스에서 effort가 지정이 안되었을때는 medium으로 보정 하도록 코드수정' (scope applied: native Codex), then '또한 ciel runtime에서 codex, codex app 등을 실행전에 toml 기본값 effort가 비어있으면 기본값을 채우는것 추가' -> plan approved ('승인'); routed-provider conflict handled with the recommended option (a): routed launches name their own effort with -c."
background: "Kobe has run gpt-6.1-sol with effort unset since 2026-10-03; Codex then uses the model catalog default (low for gpt-6.1-sol). See ../../diagnostics/aap-win/kobe-short-turns-effort-unset.okf."
changes:
  codex_config: "ciel_runtime_support/codex_config.py: codex_launch_profiles (shared with codex_config_paths_for_launch), codex_config_profile, codex_config_sets_reasoning_effort (top level or [profiles.<active>]; comments, other tables and string contents do not count)."
  config_effort: "NEW ciel_runtime_support/codex_config_effort.py: with_default_reasoning_effort (prepends 'model_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"' when the top level has none; keeps the rest byte-for-byte, CRLF and BOM), ensure_default_reasoning_effort (atomic temp-file + os.replace), codex_home_config_path (CODEX_HOME, else CLI_ASSET_HOME/.codex — the same home Ciel installs Codex prompts into; under test isolation that is the isolated config dir), ensure_logged (INFO codex_config_effort_default_written / WARN codex_config_effort_default_failed, launch continues), CodexLaunchModelSettings (prepares the config, then returns the model-settings args)."
  wiring: "ciel_runtime.py: codex_runtime_model_catalog_args = CodexLaunchModelSettings(service.runtime_model_catalog_args, os.environ, CLI_ASSET_HOME, router_log). Both runtime_launch paths (Codex TUI and app-server: remote, bare, desktop) already call it right before building the command. No port field added (architecture limits)."
  desktop: "codex_desktop_runtime.prepare_codex_home: the app's own codex-home/config.toml (seeded once) also gets the default; returns 'effort-default' in the copied list when written."
  launch_args: "codex_launch_configuration.py: native launch -> '-c model_reasoning_effort=\"medium\"' when no -c and no readable config sets it (INFO codex_reasoning_effort_default); routed launch -> '-c model_reasoning_effort=<provider effort_level or catalog default_reasoning_level>' unless a -c names the key, so a config.toml default cannot outrank the provider's effort. Behaviour change for routed: provider effort_level now wins over a hand-written top-level config effort."
  docs: "docs/Module-Map.md: codex_config, codex_config_effort (new), codex_launch_configuration."
tests:
  unit: "tests/test_codex_config_effort.py (prepend, CRLF/BOM, existing value kept, profile/other-table keys do not count, write once, missing file created, failure logged without raising, home resolution, settings prepare before args); tests/test_codex_launch_configuration.py (native default, operator choice kept, active profile, explicit -m, routed effort named / override wins / none without effort, unreadable config, remote TUI carries -c, parser cases); tests/test_codex_desktop_runtime.py (app home gets the default once, later in-app edits kept); tests/test_compaction_launch_contracts.py expectation includes the native default."
  groups: "scripts/run_test_group.py, CIEL_RUNTIME_* unset: unit OK, runtime 398 OK, router OK, channel OK; ruff clean; live router 9611 = 200; the real ~/.codex/config.toml mtime stayed 2026-10-07 23:56:41 through every run (tests write only to the isolated asset home)."
  runner_attempt: "Setting CODEX_HOME in run_test_group.py broke test_unisolated_test_guard and a channel transcript test; reverted in favour of the CLI_ASSET_HOME rule above."
e2e:
  harness: "evidence/e2e_effort.py: Ciel 'cli --ca-runtime <mode>' in its own Windows Terminal window; isolated Ciel config, CODEX_HOME (test-only API-key auth.json, models_cache.json with gpt-6.1-sol default low, trusted workspace, config.toml written by the harness with CRLF), local stub upstream recording each request body; config.toml watched every 50 ms so each distinct version is logged; one channel message via /ca/chat/notify. Codex CLI v0.161.0, Codex desktop OpenAI.Codex 26.930.3930.0."
  control: "e2e-0-control-installed-remote-unset (installed 0.2.51-nightly dbd8dae, before both changes): body {effort: low}, rollout effort=None, footer 'GPT-6.1-Sol default'."
  remote_unset: "e2e-1-remote-unset (TUI + app-server, like Kobe): config version 1 (Ciel, 15:49:51) = 'model_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"' + the original kept byte-for-byte; versions 2-3 are Codex's own tui.screen_reader_detection_done / model_availability_nux; router.log codex_config_effort_default_written; body {effort: medium}; rollout effort=medium."
  remote_high: "e2e-2-remote-high (config already 'high'): Ciel wrote nothing (0 codex_config_effort_default lines); only Codex's own two tui additions; body {effort: high}; rollout effort=high."
  tui_unset: "e2e-3-tui-unset (plain TUI, rerun alone after a contaminated first attempt): same as remote_unset; body {effort: medium}; rollout effort=medium."
  routed_high: "e2e-4-routed-high (provider vllm, effort_level high, config.toml unset): config gets the medium default, TUI command carries -c model_reasoning_effort=\"high\", rollout effort=high, footer 'Ciel Runtime vLLM high' (shots/02-after-turn.png)."
  desktop_unset: "e2e-5-desktop-unset (codex-desktop): source config gets medium at 15:53:22, desktop home prepared 15:53:23 (its config.toml has the medium line plus the app's notify entry), desktop channel turn completed via turn/start, body {effort: medium}, desktop rollout effort=medium. Screenshot shows the launcher window only; the desktop GUI itself was not captured."
not_verified:
  - "Kobe itself: needs this build installed and a relaunch; not done (no deploy/restart request)."
  - "Desktop app with an already-existing desktop home that lacks effort (unit test only; the E2E home was new and seeded from a source that already had it)."
  - "Bare app-server mode (same code path as remote; not run separately)."
incidents:
  - "Harness teardown first matched processes by run label, which also matched the bash loop driving the runs; the loop died and left one run's router/TUI running, which made the next attempt fail ('NVIDIA hosted requires an NVIDIA API key') while sharing its scratch config. Teardown now matches the run folder / scratch config path; leftovers (cmd windows of e2e-3, my own) were stopped and the scratch tree removed before the final runs."
cleanup: "E2E scratch (configs, CODEX_HOMEs, workspaces) deleted; my leftover E2E processes stopped. One Windows Terminal window titled CIELE2E-EFFORT-e2e-3-tui-unset stays open because its WindowsTerminal process also hosts other windows."
not_done: "Not committed, not pushed."
